# The .html URLs were indexed before the site moved to extensionless
# canonicals. Cloudflare's html_handling would redirect them on its own, but
# only temporarily, which leaves the old URLs sitting in Google's index. These
# explicit 301s are evaluated before html_handling and make the consolidation
# permanent. Destinations are the absolute https canonicals so Location is
# the target URL itself, not a relative path like `/` that still has to be
# resolved (and that leaves HTTP /index.html as an extra hop after the
# platform HTTPS upgrade).
/index.html        https://tinyastronomer.com/               301
/missions.html     https://tinyastronomer.com/missions       301
/scale-walk.html   https://tinyastronomer.com/scale-walk     301
/seasons.html      https://tinyastronomer.com/seasons        301
/sky-tonight.html  https://tinyastronomer.com/sky-tonight    301
/solar-system.html https://tinyastronomer.com/solar-system   301
